## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design EU-resident, privacy-conscious analytics pipelines using serverless components, ensuring tenant isolation and practical cost controls.

## Key Concepts

- API Management as secure, centralized ingress boundary
- Event Hubs for reliable, scalable ingestion
- Functions for idempotent, serverless processing
- Cosmos DB (SQL API) with tenantId partitioning and TTL for retention
- Power BI DirectQuery for near-real-time dashboards
- Azure AD RBAC for per-tenant isolation
- Key Vault-backed BYOK and encryption-at-rest
- Cost controls: autoscale, reserved capacity, budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: pseudocode for a Function that writes to Cosmos DB
const { CosmosClient } = require('@azure/cosmos');
const client = new CosmosClient(process.env.COSMOS_ENDPOINT, process.env.COSMOS_KEY);
async function handleEvent(event) {
  const tenantId = event.tenantId;
  const item = { id: event.id, tenantId, ...event.payload, ts: Date.now() };
  await client.database('TenantDb').container('Events').items.upsert(item);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency and exactly-once processing?
- How would you enforce per-tenant data residency and prevent cross-tenant access?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-region streaming, real-time analytics, security, and data sovereignty in a practical Zoom-scale scenario.

## Key Concepts

- MongoDB Atlas Change Streams to Azure Event Hubs
- Azure Databricks Spark Structured Streaming
- Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2
- Synapse for analytics and dashboards
- BYOK with Azure Key Vault
- EU residency and cross-region DR

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: subscribe to MongoDB change stream and forward to Event Hub
const { MongoClient } = require('mongodb');
const { EventHubProducerClient } = require('@azure/event-hubs');
async function streamChanges(uri, db, coll, ehConnectionString, ehName){
  const client = new MongoClient(uri);
  await client.connect();
  const collObj = client.db(db).collection(coll);
  const cursor = collObj.watch();
  const producer = new EventHubProducerClient(ehConnectionString, ehName);
  for await (const change of cursor) {
    await producer.sendBatch([{ body: change }]);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify DR failover in a test plan with sub-10s RPO?
- What changes would you make if Atlas data volume doubles?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design federated analytics with strict data residency, cross-tenant privacy, and governance in Azure at scale. It also probes edge ingestion, lakehouse patterns, federated training orchestration, and cost/DR considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Federated learning with secure aggregation and differential privacy
- Edge MQTT ingress and regional Arc gateway roles
- Delta Lake partitioning by tenant and region on ADLS Gen2
- Centralized ML registry via Azure ML; governance via Purview and BYOK
- DR with paired regions; cost controls via autoscale and quotas

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo orchestration sketch (not executable)
async function federatedStep(tenant, data) {
  ingestMQTT(tenant, data);
  streamToDelta(tenant);
  triggerFederatedTraining(tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce tenant isolation in Delta Lake at scale?
- What monitoring would you put in place for federated model drift and privacy breaches?
